  "id": "COMPOUND:43730 - PROTEIN:585",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Anhydrofurospongin-1 may interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of intermediate targets. The drug is predicted to act as a target of multiple compounds, including Labradorin 1 and 1,5-dihydroxy-6-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyxanthen-9-one, which in turn targets the same enzyme. Additionally, Anhydrofurospongin-1 is also predicted to interact with the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype, which is a target of 8-Heptadecenal, another compound that also acts on Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. These findings collectively indicate that Anhydrofurospongin-1 may exert its biological effects through a pathway involving the modulation of metabolic enzymes, particularly those involved in glycolysis. The evidence supports a potential role for Anhydrofurospongin-1 in influencing glycolytic processes, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
